WEBVTT

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:03.430
<i>Anime Ja Nai
It's not Anime!</i>

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:06.520
<i>Anime Ja Nai
It's not Anime</i>

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:11.320
<i>Hontou no koto sa
It really is real!</i>

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:13.280
<i>GUNDAM</i>

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:13.280
<i>MOBILE SUIT</i>

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.280
<i>Minna ga neshizumatta yoru
In the night when everyone else was lost in their sleep...</i>

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:18.620
<i>Mado kara sora wo miru to
I looked at the sky through the window...</i>

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:23.540
<i>Tottemo sugoi mono wo mita n' da
...and there I saw such a great thing!</i>

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.840
<i>Otona wa dare mo warai-nagara
All the adults told me with a great big laugh...</i>

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.340
<i>Terebi no misugi to iu kedo
"You've been watching way too much television again!"</i>

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.920
<i>Boku wa zettai ni zettai ni
But I would never, ever...</i>

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.140
<i>Uso nanka itte 'nai
...tell any kind of lie!</i>

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:45.520
<i>Joushiki to iu megane de
This world of ours...</i>

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:51.020
<i>Boku-tachi no sekai wa
...cannot be viewed through...</i>

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.820
<i>Nozokeya shinai no sa
...the glasses of common sense.</i>

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:58.320
<i>Yume wo wasureta
You old earthlings...</i>

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:02.830
<i>furui chikyuu-jin yo
...who have forgotten your dreams!</i>

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:07.830
<i>Anime Ja Nai! Anime Ja Nai!
It's not Anime! It's not Anime!</i>

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:10.330
<i>Fushigi na kimochi
Such a wonderful feeling!</i>

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.420
<i>Anime Ja Nai
It's not Anime!</i>

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.840
<i>Anime Ja Nai
It's not Anime!</i>

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.140
<i>Hontou no koto sa
It really is real!</i>

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:25.020
<i>Hontou no koto sa
It really is real!</i>

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:37.510
CRYBABY CECILIA

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:37.510
(Part 1)

00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:48.390
We've been ordered to
begin a new operation,

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:53.400
so the Argama has made port
at Granada to prepare for it.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:12.040
You haven't been to Anaheim
Electronics yet, have you?

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:14.040
I've been wanting to
visit at least once.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:17.420
Come along. I'll give you
a tour as a parting gift.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:18.970
W-Wait a minute...

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:23.760
Oh, Captain. After
roll call, everyone's--

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:26.510
Torres, you were on port dogwatch,
right? Don't worry about it.

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:28.100
Y-yes, sir!

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:30.180
Aren't you being too easy on him?

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:31.430
Do you think so?

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:32.600
Sorry to keep you waiting...!

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:35.350
You realize that Axis has deployed
a squadron that intends to invade Earth, right?

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:36.730
I am aware of that.

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:39.150
Haman is taking the offensive
into her own hands.

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:41.650
She intends to seize control of the
Earth while the Federation is weak.

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:45.490
That is no reason to order the
Argama to return to Earth!

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:49.970
Upon your return, I will have the new battleship
we're building at Anaheim delivered to you.

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:53.150
You people always make
your decisions on paper.

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:55.890
You don't understand the way a
crew feels about their ship.

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:57.710
And what if I do?

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:01.930
Then you think of your pilots as nothing
more than pawns in your chess game!

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:04.680
Are you talking about Kamille?

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:07.470
I guess you do remember.

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:09.590
I'm starving. Let's hurry up.

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:11.090
Wait up!

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.440
Is that him? The Newtype
that joined your crew?

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:15.900
The Newtype...?

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:19.750
Moping around on the
Argama isn't going to get Leina back to you!

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:22.730
We need to rest up and check
out Granada's local delicacy!

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:24.440
It has one?

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:27.940
Moon-face pizza! It's nice
and round, just like the moon!

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:29.780
All pizzas are round!

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:32.240
Hahah, of course they are!

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:33.410
Don't laugh at me!

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:36.050
Maybe you're just upset
because you're hungry.

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:37.290
You think so...?

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:40.470
Maybe you'll feel better if
you have something to eat!

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:45.590
Wait!

00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:46.800
What is it?

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:50.040
Do you think that maintenance on a
mobile suit is so easy to finish?

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:50.970
Mr. Wong!

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.840
I'll be right back!

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:55.600
You'll never be able to defeat
your enemies like this!

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:57.720
Where do you get off
saying this stuff, huh?

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.020
Don't flatter yourself.

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:04.900
Judau! Stop that!

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:06.960
So an adult has the right to
punch a guy outta nowhere?

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:08.820
Judau! Stop it!

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:09.780
Damn you!

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:10.900
You too, Mr. Wong!

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:13.160
You were the one that
took the first swing!

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:16.190
Stop it! Haven't you had enough?!

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:17.330
Let's go!

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:20.460
Well then, I guess we'll
also be... W-what is it?

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:21.420
Captain!

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:23.080
Head back to the Argama!

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:24.170
What about Beecha and the guys?

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:25.500
They'll be fine without us.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:26.710
Sheesh!

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:36.390
I lived here till I was around ten years
old, but I've never heard of this place.

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:38.310
Oh, so you're from around here?

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:41.230
Yeah. I'd spend more time
here if I had my way.

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:45.640
You've heard the talk about going
to Earth, huh? That must be rough.

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:48.400
Leaving you behind is the
roughest part of it, Miss Milly.

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:52.110
- Oh, a smooth talker! My treat, then.
- Thanks!

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:54.330
- All right!
- Thanks for the food!

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:55.700
Why are you two here?!

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:57.910
It's been awhile, Miss Milly!

00:04:57.910 --> 00:04:59.890
Did you talk to Mr. Wong?

00:04:59.890 --> 00:05:01.840
Something like that.

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:04.880
"Something like"... Oh, you didn't!

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:05.880
Torres!

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:07.040
Where's Cecilia?

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:09.510
She screwed up again.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:13.220
That's enough! Back to work!

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:14.430
I'm terribly sorry.

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:17.970
Cecilia, someone's calling
for you! Table five!

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:21.520
Milly...

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:26.190
I know what I want on the pizza,
so just pick something to drink.

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:27.400
S-Sure...

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:29.190
Miss Milly... it's been a while.

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:30.860
I'm doing okay. And you?

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:33.320
I felt pretty lonely
since you've been gone so long.

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:36.550
Lately, I've been seriously thinking
about escaping to a colony.

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:38.660
Moving again?

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:40.370
Yeah, to a colony this time.

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:41.540
C'mon, take our order!

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:42.390
Yup, yup.

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:46.500
Oh. One Granada moon-face
pizza and three colas.

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:48.470
The cola here isn't salty, right?

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:50.550
Torres!

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:52.060
Is that Torres?!

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:55.340
I-I'm sorry.

00:05:55.340 --> 00:05:56.010
Strike!

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:56.840
You're out!

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:59.690
You really are the ever-clumsy
Cecilia the Crybaby.

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:01.010
Crybaby?

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:02.140
T-Torres!

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:03.060
Yeah...

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:05.940
Y-You were called
Torres the Weak, too!

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:08.570
Torres the Weak?

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:15.950
We stand out too much here....
Let's go around to the back.

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:17.860
Then, I'll go tell my big sister.

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:19.950
Nel, Creyu, you two can go back.

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:20.660
Yes, sir!

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:22.880
What kind of idiot salutes
in a place like this?!

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:25.460
Return immediately and
prepare for the operation!

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:27.830
Make sure you're able to plant
explosives at any moment!

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:29.630
Um... what about food?

00:06:29.630 --> 00:06:33.630
Take care of that somewhere around
here! The Argama won't be waiting for us!

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:34.300
Yes, sir!

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:35.600
Don't do that!

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:37.970
Sis!

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:41.100
Pete, you shouldn't be here! What
about taking care of Grandma?!

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:43.500
The third-oldest sister
is looking after her.

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:46.780
I guided them here,
and they gave me this!

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:51.440
They said it was money
good even in Side 6.

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:54.070
Hurry home now. You
have to make dinner, right?

00:06:54.070 --> 00:06:55.490
Yeah!

00:06:58.000 --> 00:06:59.320
I-I'm sorry.

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:01.910
I'll get the rest of the
money before we depart.

00:07:01.910 --> 00:07:04.260
So please don't cancel our
seats on the immigration ship.

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:06.250
You punched Mr. Wong?!

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:09.020
Who's even left who could
pay 10,000 gilla to leave?

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:11.420
Yeah, I bet the rich people
all left a long time ago.

00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:13.340
Don't try to change the subject!

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:16.300
Look, he was the one
who punched me first.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:18.170
Go back and apologize
to him right now, Judau.

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:19.010
Why?

00:07:19.010 --> 00:07:23.350
That man... has tremendous
influence in the AEUG.

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:27.020
So, he's the boss of the AEUG?

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:30.780
Enough! We don't know where
enemy spies might be hiding!

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:32.400
We have no choice but to eat here.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:33.480
But, still...

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:35.690
Come on! Let's all go
apologize to Mr. Wong!

00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:37.190
I'm still eating!

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:40.580
If they kick you off the ship, you
won't be able to go rescue Leina!

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:45.290
You shouldn't eat so fast.

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:46.460
Judau.

00:07:48.930 --> 00:07:50.170
What's that?

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:51.420
Huh?

00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:57.260
Are you all right?

00:07:57.260 --> 00:07:59.420
WHEW! Finally got it down!

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:02.010
What are you going to do? Are
you going to go apologize?

00:08:02.010 --> 00:08:04.470
Why the hell should I go
over there and apologize?!

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:06.210
What do I need to do?

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:07.990
What's wrong?

00:08:07.990 --> 00:08:09.890
This doesn't involve
life-threatening danger.

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:11.850
But my family...

00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:13.790
I understand that. That's why...

00:08:13.790 --> 00:08:15.450
Judau?

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:20.620
Oh, my...

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:23.280
I can't possibly do
something like that.

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:27.670
At this rate, the immigration ship may
charge a fee for breach of contract.

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:31.840
W-What is it?

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:33.750
A down payment and a camera.

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:36.090
Once you take a shot of
the map, bring it to me.

00:08:36.090 --> 00:08:39.670
I'll give you money and tickets for an
immigration ship that departs tomorrow.

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:43.180
I'll meet you immediately if you go to
Port Blan and say that your name is Candy.

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:44.570
At the edge of town?

00:08:44.570 --> 00:08:47.690
The more you hurry, the
more money you'll make.

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:51.180
He's trying to make
her do some spy work!

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:52.270
I have to stop her!

00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:54.560
Even if we catch her now,
we won't have any evidence.

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:56.750
Besides, if we could
catch her red-handed...

00:08:56.750 --> 00:08:59.780
You're going to frame her?
But she's Torres's friend!

00:08:59.780 --> 00:09:02.530
Don't you want to show Mr. Wong up?!

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:04.200
This is your chance, Judau.

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:05.240
Hey, aren't you done yet?

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:06.710
Not yet!

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:09.700
I'm sure they're up to no good.

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:10.790
Torres?

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:12.550
Were you sobbing again?

00:09:12.550 --> 00:09:16.260
I-I'm sorry, I got a sudden errand
to run, so I have to go home now.

00:09:16.850 --> 00:09:18.770
Come by sometime in
the evening or something.

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:22.810
You still remember where it is, right?
It's a pretty filthy place, though.

00:09:23.530 --> 00:09:26.640
What happened to you?!
You look really pale!

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:28.630
No, it's nothing.

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:33.320
Back when you were a kid, Cecilia, you
always tried to hide things that were bothering you.

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:35.520
Don't hide this from me!

00:09:38.710 --> 00:09:39.660
Huh?

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:43.820
Two slices of moon-face pizza, the
local delicacy of Granada! Hurry it up!

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:46.240
And we'll have two more slices of
moonface pizza, too!

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:47.710
Wow, it's popular--

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:53.040
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:56.210
It's Nel and Creyu. After all
the times they overworked us...

00:09:56.210 --> 00:09:57.790
Thank you very much.

00:09:57.790 --> 00:10:01.770
If we don't get back to Port
Blan soon, Gottn's gonna yell at us again.

00:10:01.770 --> 00:10:04.100
Port Blan?

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:05.410
I don't like it.

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:09.110
You really think we can surprise the
Argama? Our spy's just a civilian...

00:10:09.110 --> 00:10:10.390
A surprise attack on the Argama?!

00:10:10.390 --> 00:10:13.420
Come over here, Beecha, Mondo!

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:14.600
Miss Milly?!

00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:15.640
You guys?!

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:16.820
You heard us!

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:18.000
YOU!

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:19.820
You're not getting away!

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:22.650
What in the world is going on?!

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:23.820
Manager!

00:10:23.820 --> 00:10:24.990
What is it?!

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:26.610
Judau, we have to stop them!

00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:27.200
Yeah.

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:28.250
OUCH!

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:29.870
Where do you think you're going?!

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:31.660
That's an illegal move!

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:33.040
No rules in a fight!

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:34.450
Creyu! Let's go!

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:35.840
Yeah!

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:38.130
You're not getting away!

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:43.250
Don't follow them!

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:44.210
Why's that?

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:45.760
We have to let the Argama know first!

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:49.190
If we don't stop that attack, it'll
turn Granada into a sea of flames!

00:10:50.570 --> 00:10:51.550
Judau?!

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:53.150
Follow that Ele-car!

00:10:53.150 --> 00:10:54.850
We're gonna go to the Argama!

00:10:54.850 --> 00:10:56.180
That's fine!

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:56.730
What?

00:10:56.730 --> 00:10:58.070
Let's go!

00:10:58.750 --> 00:11:00.620
Hey! Wait!

00:11:00.620 --> 00:11:01.690
You guys!

00:11:01.690 --> 00:11:03.070
What's wrong?

00:11:03.070 --> 00:11:04.280
That's what I'd like to know!

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:06.830
And this was our farewell
pizza party, too!

00:11:07.300 --> 00:11:08.960
Torres!

00:11:11.090 --> 00:11:12.030
What's up?

00:11:12.030 --> 00:11:12.870
It's all right.

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:14.240
Elle! Stay low!

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:16.620
Geez, legs to yourself!

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:18.040
Hurry up and pass that thing!

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:19.220
I know that!

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:24.340
It's not that she's really
beautiful or anything, right?

00:11:24.340 --> 00:11:26.680
Yeah. Elle is prettier.

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:28.980
Idiot!

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:37.870
Halt!

00:11:37.870 --> 00:11:41.400
U-Um, I'd like to go to
the ship named Argama.

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:42.360
Where's your clearance pass?

00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:46.110
Um, nobody gave me
anything like that.

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:48.240
If you don't have one, you
can't go any further.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:51.500
I was told to deliver a pizza.
You know our place, right?

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:54.120
You've eaten at our
place before, right?

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:56.670
You're the girl from that
place. I know your face.

00:11:56.670 --> 00:12:00.290
I beg you! If it gets cold, it'll
be bad for our reputation.

00:12:00.290 --> 00:12:02.050
I'll have someone from
the Argama come out.

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:15.930
That's for sure?

00:12:15.930 --> 00:12:18.140
I don't know! I'll go
talk to the captain.

00:12:18.140 --> 00:12:21.940
Please do! We'll be prepping
at the mobile-suit deck.

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:27.190
Mr. Wong, do you really think that Beecha
and Mondo have no place in this crew?

00:12:27.190 --> 00:12:30.240
How can we trust people who
have betrayed us before?!

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:31.950
Right?

00:12:32.760 --> 00:12:37.290
That wasn't betrayal. It just proves
that they have overwhelming power.

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:39.160
Are you saying they're Newtypes?

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:41.210
Those kids are a far cry
from someone like Kamille!

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:43.750
They're different people,
so they act differently.

00:12:43.750 --> 00:12:46.880
The way a Cyber-Newtype is different
than a Newtype, I'm sure.

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:50.360
That's going too far! Those kids are
already part of the Argama's crew.

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:53.420
What's the old man yelling
about this time?

00:12:53.420 --> 00:12:56.970
You've never been on a battlefield,
so you don't understand.

00:12:56.970 --> 00:12:59.200
They're fighting the
only way they know how.

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:02.110
I understand everything about
those two, and your Judau Ashta!

00:13:02.110 --> 00:13:05.310
I don't need a soldier who only
fights to save his little sister.

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:07.270
I want soldiers who fight
for the goals of the AEUG!

00:13:07.270 --> 00:13:08.150
Mr. Wong...

00:13:08.150 --> 00:13:09.660
I've heard enough!

00:13:10.130 --> 00:13:11.340
Judau?

00:13:11.340 --> 00:13:14.700
What part of saving my
little sister is bad?

00:13:14.700 --> 00:13:19.490
Are you saying that your weird war is
worth more than my little sister's life?!

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:20.370
Judau!

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:21.700
You shut up, Captain!

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:24.000
You don't understand anything!

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:25.710
Yeah, I don't undestand!

00:13:25.710 --> 00:13:28.460
You just watch. I'm going
to rescue Leina on my own!

00:13:28.460 --> 00:13:30.170
Judau, where do you
think you're going?!

00:13:30.170 --> 00:13:31.340
Wha? Pizza?

00:13:31.340 --> 00:13:32.130
Huh?

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:34.050
A pizza delivery? That
can wait till later!

00:13:34.050 --> 00:13:35.180
What the...

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:36.090
What's going on?

00:13:36.090 --> 00:13:37.470
He said, "That can wait till later!"

00:13:37.470 --> 00:13:39.680
Huh? That's Elle.

00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:41.980
What are you doing, Elle?

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:45.310
An emergency buzzer?

00:13:45.310 --> 00:13:46.400
I-I'm sorry!

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:47.020
H-Hey...

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:50.280
The Argama told you to wait.

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:53.040
It's gotten cold now, so
I'll bring a new one later!

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:54.110
Cecilia?!

00:13:54.110 --> 00:13:55.330
You gotta stop her!

00:13:56.460 --> 00:13:58.320
I wonder if we can
get out of this port.

00:13:58.320 --> 00:14:00.830
That's why Judau went
up onto the bridge!

00:14:01.010 --> 00:14:04.050
Beam rifle, check! I'm launching!

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:06.420
The Mk. II!?

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:08.670
Who is it? We just finished
maintenance on it!

00:14:08.670 --> 00:14:11.670
We've gotta stop the Axis spy!
We know where she's going!

00:14:11.670 --> 00:14:12.510
A spy?

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:13.860
Is that you, Mondo?

00:14:13.860 --> 00:14:15.050
And Beecha in the Zeta?

00:14:15.050 --> 00:14:18.470
We gotta score some points here
or nobody is gonna trust us, right?

00:14:18.700 --> 00:14:20.510
Does Captain Bright know about this?

00:14:20.510 --> 00:14:23.530
We're headed to the port
that the spy is using!

00:14:23.530 --> 00:14:24.930
This better be the truth!

00:14:24.930 --> 00:14:27.480
It's true! Please open the
hatch for the mobile-suit deck!

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:28.310
Roger!

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:32.820
Iino, I know I've caused you a lot of grief...
You stay straight from here on out!

00:14:32.980 --> 00:14:34.240
What do you mean?

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:35.240
Hurry, get the hatch!

00:14:35.240 --> 00:14:36.790
Oh, right!

00:14:38.630 --> 00:14:40.910
Are you going to run away
using the Double Zeta?!

00:14:40.910 --> 00:14:42.660
Rude doesn't even begin
to describe this!

00:14:42.660 --> 00:14:46.500
We gotta crush the spy that wants
to infiltrate the Argama, right?

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:48.210
I'm gonna go out there
and do it myself!

00:14:48.210 --> 00:14:49.630
So quit trash talking me!

00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:51.090
You're just making that up!

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:52.260
No!

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:56.470
He's not the type who'd lie just
to lay hands on a mobile suit.

00:14:58.780 --> 00:15:00.260
I bet Wong was surprised!

00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:01.050
Like I would know!

00:15:01.050 --> 00:15:02.100
You didn't talk to him?

00:15:02.320 --> 00:15:04.310
I'm gonna take down
the entire enemy ship!

00:15:04.310 --> 00:15:06.680
Even if I gotta do it by myself,
I will get Leina back!

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:09.060
Shut down the port exit
and capture those three!

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:11.610
No. Caesar! I understand
what's going on now!

00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:12.730
Captain!

00:15:12.730 --> 00:15:14.980
You're the one who doesn't understand.

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:16.610
Open the port hatch!

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:18.740
I don't have to open it for them!

00:15:18.740 --> 00:15:20.700
There is an ongoing emergency
alarm down at the port.

00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:22.530
Right now, mobile suits can
launch freely.

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:26.660
All right! All mechanics assigned to the
Argama's refit, stop work!

00:15:26.660 --> 00:15:27.660
Why?!

00:15:27.660 --> 00:15:30.800
Class-two battle stations!
Light up the main engine!

00:15:31.310 --> 00:15:36.330
You're going to believe everything
those children say? How naive.

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:39.380
You've been waiting for the
emergence of Newtypes.

00:15:39.380 --> 00:15:43.640
So why can't you believe that these
children may understand things we don't?

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:47.180
Don't you think their insights are the
beginnings of Newtype perception?

00:15:47.180 --> 00:15:49.780
- But...
- Am I speaking too freely?

00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:54.870
Zeta! Beecha, launching!

00:15:55.940 --> 00:15:58.410
What amazing power!

00:15:58.410 --> 00:15:59.750
I'm going ahead!

00:16:02.340 --> 00:16:05.330
Man, how can you make the
Double Zeta move like that?

00:16:05.330 --> 00:16:07.160
You're not exactly doing
bad yourself, Beecha!

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:10.300
Oh, it's 'cause I spent a lot of time
in the simulator back on the Endra.

00:16:16.060 --> 00:16:18.170
This is a tight squeeze.

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:27.640
There isn't much
distance, right, Beecha?

00:16:27.640 --> 00:16:29.110
You should be able to see it soon!

00:16:38.460 --> 00:16:40.110
Launching Gaza-C and Ga-Zowmn units.

00:16:40.110 --> 00:16:42.610
I have not authorized
an attack! Stop them!

00:16:42.610 --> 00:16:44.530
The enemy knows our location!

00:16:44.530 --> 00:16:46.490
We're going to crush the Argama
with an all-out attack!

00:16:46.490 --> 00:16:47.830
You can't!

00:16:47.830 --> 00:16:51.830
We have to win Granada without civilian casualties
or we'll be too ashamed to look Lady Haman in the face!

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:53.670
But the enemy has arrived!

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:54.580
What?

00:16:54.580 --> 00:16:56.090
There are three units in our sector!

00:16:56.090 --> 00:16:58.210
How the hell did they find us?!

00:16:58.210 --> 00:17:00.090
Nel, Creyu, get out there!

00:17:00.090 --> 00:17:01.920
R-Roger. We'll take
responsibility for this!

00:17:01.920 --> 00:17:04.020
Responsibility? What
are you talking about?

00:17:07.990 --> 00:17:10.020
We could pick 'em off from
here, before they launch!

00:17:10.200 --> 00:17:13.440
Wait! If we wreck the port, there
won't be a ship left for me to use!

00:17:13.440 --> 00:17:15.950
Huh? What are you thinking?

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:19.110
I've been kicked off the Argama, so...

00:17:19.110 --> 00:17:22.040
I'm going to take an enemy ship
and use that to go rescue Leina.

00:17:22.550 --> 00:17:26.030
So what are you holding back
for, Judau? Go get 'em!

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:31.370
Mondo!

00:17:31.370 --> 00:17:32.580
I-It just grazed me!

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:34.380
How dare you!

00:17:36.640 --> 00:17:39.930
Nel! Keep that Gundam busy!

00:17:40.650 --> 00:17:42.390
Not gonna let you!

00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:44.310
What?!

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:53.310
You idiots! Who in their right
mind fights right above the hatch?!

00:17:53.310 --> 00:17:55.110
Tell them to get away from there!

00:17:57.040 --> 00:17:58.650
Are you trying to destroy the port?!

00:17:58.650 --> 00:18:01.070
At this rate, we won't be
able to launch the ship.

00:18:01.070 --> 00:18:04.200
Wait for an opening and launch!
Do you want to get us killed?!

00:18:06.240 --> 00:18:07.790
So fast!

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:13.130
I'm not letting you get away!

00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:17.380
I won't even need to use my beam rifle!

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:21.090
L-Let go of me!

00:18:21.090 --> 00:18:24.630
I'm not letting you go! How dare you
treat the two of us like slaves!

00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:26.350
Y-You're...!

00:18:27.190 --> 00:18:30.440
We're not letting you destroy
Granada on top of that!

00:18:33.140 --> 00:18:35.150
One more shot!

00:18:35.580 --> 00:18:38.350
S-Stop it! You're crushing us!

00:18:38.350 --> 00:18:39.990
We're trying to crush you!

00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:44.790
Help us!

00:18:47.210 --> 00:18:49.040
YOU!

00:18:50.970 --> 00:18:54.830
Are you the one who let
them know our location?!

00:18:54.830 --> 00:18:59.880
I did no such thing! I even found the
Argama at Granada Port...

00:19:03.100 --> 00:19:05.340
You figured out where the Argama is?!

00:19:05.340 --> 00:19:07.170
I got a picture of the
guard-station map...

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:09.360
But nothing was written down.

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:12.050
Then, go do it again! One more time!

00:19:12.050 --> 00:19:13.510
B-But I'm scared!

00:19:13.510 --> 00:19:16.910
If you don't, you'll be dragged
into this battle, and you will die!

00:19:16.910 --> 00:19:19.900
I'll tell you where to
contact me at your house!

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:23.530
Cecilia!

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:25.440
And this wraps up...

00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:26.990
our sweet revenge!

00:19:26.990 --> 00:19:28.750
Here we go!

00:19:31.420 --> 00:19:33.620
I'm going to use the beam saber!

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:36.700
If I die here, I won't be able
to eat my mom's cooking anymore!

00:19:36.700 --> 00:19:38.210
Mom...?

00:19:43.350 --> 00:19:45.420
You're too easy, Double Zeta!

00:19:45.420 --> 00:19:48.050
To think that you'd get all shaken
up over hearing "mom"!

00:19:48.050 --> 00:19:49.890
Did he get away?

00:19:52.570 --> 00:19:54.560
You half-assed...!

00:20:07.380 --> 00:20:10.250
T-The ship... is it all right?

00:20:13.130 --> 00:20:16.950
It's all right, Judau. For now,
we defeated their mobile suits.

00:20:16.950 --> 00:20:19.750
I'm sure even Mr. Wong won't be
screaming his head off over it.

00:20:19.750 --> 00:20:24.340
Yeah... I'd like to think
that, but.... that man...

00:20:28.020 --> 00:20:30.880
Do you know exactly
what you did out there?

00:20:30.880 --> 00:20:32.130
We defeated the enemy!

00:20:32.130 --> 00:20:35.140
That was a coincidence! It obviously
wasn't the result of your skills alone.

00:20:35.140 --> 00:20:36.010
What was that?!

00:20:36.010 --> 00:20:37.850
Maybe you need an attitude adjustment!

00:20:37.850 --> 00:20:41.890
I didn't do any of this for you,
so if you don't like it, then go ahead!

00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:43.230
I'll go with him.

00:20:43.230 --> 00:20:45.440
- Me too!
- Me too!

00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:46.440
Me too!

00:20:46.650 --> 00:20:47.980
All of you...

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:51.280
How you punish these
children is up to you.

00:20:51.280 --> 00:20:57.630
But please do not forget that the entire
crew of the Argama feels exactly as they do.

00:20:58.220 --> 00:20:59.880
Captain...

00:21:07.100 --> 00:21:10.380
I don't know when the next war
is going to break out,

00:21:10.380 --> 00:21:12.470
so I just wanted to escape
from this place.

00:21:14.190 --> 00:21:16.930
Wipe your tears... Calm down.

00:21:16.930 --> 00:21:18.520
Torres...

00:21:20.870 --> 00:21:24.350
If you need to leave, I can
lend you some money.

00:21:24.350 --> 00:21:27.200
I need enough for seven
people... That's impossible.

00:21:28.290 --> 00:21:32.860
Torres, you always treated
me like this when I cried.

00:21:32.860 --> 00:21:35.040
I-Is that so?

00:21:39.970 --> 00:21:43.040
Hey, Torres... join me
on the immigration ship.

00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:45.220
Let's escape together,
just like old times.

00:21:45.220 --> 00:21:49.090
Torres, if you stay
here, you'll die, too.

00:21:49.090 --> 00:21:51.880
But what'll you do if they decide
to kick us off the ship?

00:21:51.880 --> 00:21:55.230
It'll be fine. I'll find my
own way to go rescue Leina.

00:21:56.240 --> 00:21:59.500
- You'll run away?
- No!

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:00.820
Torres?

00:22:00.820 --> 00:22:02.430
H-Hey, guys.

00:22:02.430 --> 00:22:03.520
What are you doing?

00:22:03.520 --> 00:22:05.810
I just thought I'd try
to calm her down a bit.

00:22:05.810 --> 00:22:07.230
I'm going home.

00:22:07.230 --> 00:22:08.610
Cecilia!

00:22:08.610 --> 00:22:09.650
You can't!

00:22:09.650 --> 00:22:10.690
W-Why?!

00:22:10.690 --> 00:22:12.160
Because!

00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:14.360
Torres...

00:22:14.360 --> 00:22:15.650
What's wrong with Cecilia?

00:22:15.650 --> 00:22:18.540
Judau... you've gotta explain.

00:22:18.970 --> 00:22:20.250
Elle...

00:22:20.840 --> 00:22:23.460
Judau... what's going on?

00:22:25.720 --> 00:22:27.260
That woman...

00:22:29.350 --> 00:22:31.100
She--

00:22:46.100 --> 00:22:51.770
<i>michi mo nai areta genya ni
Amidst the wasteland without any roads...</i>

00:22:53.280 --> 00:22:58.990
<i>reeru wo tsukuru no wa kurushii koto sa
...it's difficult to lay down your rails.</i>

00:23:01.200 --> 00:23:03.490
<i>dakedo
However...</i>

00:23:03.490 --> 00:23:09.790
<i>tooi mukou mo shiranakucha ikenai
You've gotta know what's on the other side...</i>

00:23:09.790 --> 00:23:16.880
<i>boku-tachi wa kore kara nanda
...it's all from here on for us.</i>

00:23:16.880 --> 00:23:21.300
<i>"yume wo wasureta kodomo-tachi" to
"Children will forget their dreams"...</i>

00:23:21.300 --> 00:23:23.680
<i>hito wa iu
...is what they say.</i>

00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:33.900
<i>aa jidai ga naiteiru
Ah, the times are crying.</i>

00:23:45.700 --> 00:23:49.530
If you start trouble, you have
to settle the score yourself.

00:23:49.530 --> 00:23:53.230
But Gottn gave Cecilia a bomb!

00:23:53.230 --> 00:23:55.490
You know, in the vacuum of space,

00:23:55.490 --> 00:23:57.510
you can't easily throw
something like that away.

00:23:57.510 --> 00:24:00.450
Cecilia does her best
for Torres's sake,

00:24:00.450 --> 00:24:02.840
but working hard for the
wrong side is a mistake!

00:24:02.840 --> 00:24:04.730
Throw away that briefcase!

00:24:04.730 --> 00:24:07.870
CRYBABY CECILIA

00:24:04.730 --> 00:24:07.870
(Part 2)

00:24:04.730 --> 00:24:07.870
Next Time

00:24:04.750 --> 00:24:08.920
Next time on Gundam ZZ:
"Cecilia the Crybaby."

00:24:08.920 --> 00:24:11.160
It continues today's story,
so it'll be salty!
